[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3247443544","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/110215#issuecomment-3247443544","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/110215","id":3247443544,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7BkA5Y","user":{"login":"WhalesState","id":53877170,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUzODc3MTcw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/53877170?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/WhalesState","html_url":"https://github.com/WhalesState","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WhalesState/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WhalesState/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WhalesState/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WhalesState/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WhalesState/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WhalesState/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WhalesState/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WhalesState/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WhalesState/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-09-03T02:12:29Z","updated_at":"2025-09-03T02:12:29Z","body":"Can't we just make `ImageTexture::set_image()` accepts null values to clear the image instead of throwing Errors ?\r\n\r\nAnyways, this mimics the old behavior without those annoying errors when duplicating themes which contains empty `ImageTexture` resources.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3247443544/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3249778643","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/110215#issuecomment-3249778643","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/110215","id":3249778643,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7Bs6_T","user":{"login":"RandomShaper","id":11797174,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjExNzk3MTc0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/11797174?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/RandomShaper","html_url":"https://github.com/RandomShaper","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RandomShaper/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RandomShaper/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RandomShaper/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RandomShaper/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RandomShaper/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RandomShaper/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RandomShaper/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RandomShaper/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RandomShaper/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-09-03T15:41:51Z","updated_at":"2025-09-03T15:41:51Z","body":"> Can't we just make `ImageTexture::set_image()` accepts null values to clear the image instead of throwing Errors ?\r\n\r\nThat's the route I'd favor.\r\n\r\nIn my opinion, the classic behavior had an asymmetry we'd better get rid of as part of the tidying of duplicate semantics. If a given getter can return a null reference, the corresponding setter should be fine with null as well. Therefore, I agree `ImageTexture::set_image()` should work as described.\r\n\r\nMoreover, if we reinstated the old behavior of not assigning a null resource, we could have the following situation:\r\n- Resource class `CoolRes` has a resource property for which it creates a resource as the default value.\r\n- An instance of `CoolRes` has that property set to null.\r\n- Such instance is duplicated, but you get the default value instead of null.\r\n\r\nI think that would challenge expectations.\r\n\r\n@WhalesState, do you think you could implement the lenient `set_image()` approach?","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3249778643/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3250153389","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/110215#issuecomment-3250153389","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/110215","id":3250153389,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7BuWet","user":{"login":"WhalesState","id":53877170,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUzODc3MTcw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/53877170?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/WhalesState","html_url":"https://github.com/WhalesState","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WhalesState/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WhalesState/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WhalesState/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WhalesState/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WhalesState/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WhalesState/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WhalesState/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WhalesState/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WhalesState/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-09-03T17:32:21Z","updated_at":"2025-09-03T17:34:24Z","body":"> @WhalesState, do you think you could implement the lenient `set_image()` approach?\r\n\r\nI can allow `set_image()` to clear the image when a null or empty image is passed but this will break compatibility since the old behavior protects the image once set, another way which i may prefer is to return silently, also we have `PROPERTY_USAGE_RESOURCE_NOT_PERSISTENT` added here https://github.com/fire/godot/commit/0960f46b0bac8b721cd5863b1b7430f7a2e767e4 which is only used for `ImageTexture::image`, `ImageTextureLayered::_images` and `ImageTexture3D::_images` and we can use to continue while duplicating if the value is null. I'd prefer the last solution to avoid breaking compatibility.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3250153389/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3250294445","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/110215#issuecomment-3250294445","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/110215","id":3250294445,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7Bu46t","user":{"login":"RandomShaper","id":11797174,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjExNzk3MTc0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/11797174?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/RandomShaper","html_url":"https://github.com/RandomShaper","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RandomShaper/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RandomShaper/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RandomShaper/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RandomShaper/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RandomShaper/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RandomShaper/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RandomShaper/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RandomShaper/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RandomShaper/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-09-03T18:22:06Z","updated_at":"2025-09-03T18:22:06Z","body":"Makes sense.\r\n\r\nAside, instead of having a composite return type, I'd suggest using a `bool &r_valid` parameter. I'm not opposed on principle to richer return values, but I think those are a bit alient to the codebase, where the more spartan output parameters have a stronger tradition.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3250294445/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3250736180","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/110215#issuecomment-3250736180","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/110215","id":3250736180,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7Bwkw0","user":{"login":"WhalesState","id":53877170,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUzODc3MTcw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/53877170?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/WhalesState","html_url":"https://github.com/WhalesState","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WhalesState/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WhalesState/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WhalesState/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WhalesState/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WhalesState/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WhalesState/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WhalesState/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WhalesState/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WhalesState/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-09-03T20:45:38Z","updated_at":"2025-09-03T20:45:38Z","body":"I have fixed it inside `image_texture.cpp` Instead of complicating and slowing down the resources duplication.\r\n\r\nThe main issue was that we can initialize empty `ImageTexture` and `ImageTexture3D` but while duplicating it tries to set the images again to null.\r\n\r\nYou can test the old behavior with this script.\r\n\r\n```gdscript\r\n@tool\r\nextends Control\r\n\r\nfunc _ready():\r\n\tvar layered = ImageTexture3D.new()\r\n\tvar _layered = layered.duplicate(true)\r\n\tvar time = Time.get_ticks_msec()\r\n\tvar _new_theme = ThemeDB.get_default_theme().duplicate(true)\r\n\tprint(Time.get_ticks_msec() - time)\r\n\tvar image_texture = ImageTexture.new()\r\n\tvar _new_texture = image_texture.duplicate()\r\n```","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3250736180/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3257946582","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/110215#issuecomment-3257946582","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/110215","id":3257946582,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7CMFHW","user":{"login":"RandomShaper","id":11797174,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjExNzk3MTc0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/11797174?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/RandomShaper","html_url":"https://github.com/RandomShaper","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RandomShaper/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RandomShaper/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RandomShaper/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RandomShaper/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RandomShaper/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RandomShaper/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RandomShaper/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RandomShaper/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RandomShaper/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-09-05T10:57:57Z","updated_at":"2025-09-05T10:57:57Z","body":"Nice approach. If anything, `resource.cpp` can be left untouched.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3257946582/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3257956575","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/110215#issuecomment-3257956575","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/110215","id":3257956575,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7CMHjf","user":{"login":"WhalesState","id":53877170,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUzODc3MTcw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/53877170?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/WhalesState","html_url":"https://github.com/WhalesState","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WhalesState/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WhalesState/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WhalesState/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WhalesState/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WhalesState/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WhalesState/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WhalesState/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WhalesState/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WhalesState/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-09-05T11:02:03Z","updated_at":"2025-09-05T19:18:00Z","body":"> Nice approach. If anything, `resource.cpp` can be left untouched.\r\n\r\n<img width=\"660\" height=\"894\" alt=\"image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/143b7552-910a-4e20-8548-39d9ef6c7d9c\" />\r\n\r\nIf the resource is not valid, we don't need `should_duplicate` variable since it will not be changed and it will always have an extra check to see if it's true then it jumps to `return p_variant`. I have kept this change since it will make all null `Object`s return faster.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3257956575/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":{"reason":"resolved"}},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3258733214","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/110215#issuecomment-3258733214","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/110215","id":3258733214,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7CPFKe","user":{"login":"RandomShaper","id":11797174,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjExNzk3MTc0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/11797174?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/RandomShaper","html_url":"https://github.com/RandomShaper","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RandomShaper/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RandomShaper/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RandomShaper/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RandomShaper/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RandomShaper/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RandomShaper/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RandomShaper/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RandomShaper/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RandomShaper/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-09-05T15:16:34Z","updated_at":"2025-09-05T15:16:34Z","body":"The code was written like that on purpose. That way, you can read it as having two stages: 1) determine duplicatability, 2) duplicate or skip based on that.\r\n\r\nThe early return is a stylistic change as far as I can tell, with probably not everyone agreeing on which is better.\r\n\r\nIf it comes with a measurable performance gain, I'd say it'd belong in a separate PR anyway.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3258733214/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3259475331","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/110215#issuecomment-3259475331","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/110215","id":3259475331,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7CR6WD","user":{"login":"WhalesState","id":53877170,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUzODc3MTcw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/53877170?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/WhalesState","html_url":"https://github.com/WhalesState","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WhalesState/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WhalesState/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WhalesState/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WhalesState/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WhalesState/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WhalesState/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WhalesState/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WhalesState/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WhalesState/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-09-05T19:17:22Z","updated_at":"2025-09-05T19:17:22Z","body":"> The code was written like that on purpose. That way, you can read it as having two stages: 1) determine duplicatability, 2) duplicate or skip based on that.\r\n\r\nReverted the change.\r\n\r\n","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3259475331/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3267566316","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/110215#issuecomment-3267566316","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/110215","id":3267566316,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7Cwxrs","user":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/received_events","